0 Die Säule, 1949 - three tubeless bricks stacked, and it does not hold (A3-S04)
0 Name: saeule.ldr
0 Author: spex project (hand-authored placement data; not sourced from an official ldraw.org models/ release)
0 // Three of `parts/abb-2x2.dat`, stacked. This is the 1949 object:
0 // sharp-cornered and flat-studded, where Page's was rounded and bobbled;
0 // studs on top, hollow underneath, and nothing inside to grip them. The
0 // column stands because it is stacked, not because it is clutched - which
0 // is the whole reason the next shot exists.
0 //
0 // A rebuild rather than a morph, the same grammar A2-S02 used for the bulla
0 // and A3-S04 for the first column: the three separate bricks dissolve out
0 // while this dissolves in. Nothing in this piece transforms into anything.
0 //
0 // Stage position x = 20720 LDU (1036 studs). Brick 24 LDU tall, origin at
0 // the footprint centre, LDraw +Y down.
1 15 20720 -24 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 abb-2x2.dat
